we can only imagine just how long it  would take to plow through all of  Netflix as many movies documentaries and  TV shows months maybe or even years with  so many titles available to subscribers  it can be easy to get a little  overwhelmed by everything the streaming  service has to offer luckily we've  compiled this list of a few of Netflix's  finest hidden gems the perfect go twos  next time you find yourself at a loss  for what to watch beyond skyline B  movies usually tend to get a fairly bad  rap thanks to their lower than average  budgets questionable performances and  poor scripts and let's be honest beyond  skyline fits snugly into pretty much all  of those categories the basic plot is  this aliens invade earth using a bunch  of high-tech blue lights which turn  people into zombies allowing said aliens  to harvest their brains enter Frank  Grillo as mark an alcoholic cop whose  principal method for dealing with the  aliens can be largely summed up as  punching them until they go away  so yes it sounds like your typical  b-movie dud but beyond skyline is  clearly a labor of love the movies  attention to detail betrays a passion on  the part of the filmmakers that you  struggle to even find in many of today's  big budget blockbusters also it's a lot  of fun if you've got a soft spot for  genre movies you'll have a blast  the boy on the surface the boy appears  to be your average run-of-the-mill  horror movie it's about a young American  nanny who takes a job caring for the son  of an elderly couple in the English  countryside she thinks they're playing a  joke when she discovers that their son  is actually a porcelain doll named  Brahms but soon begins to suspect that  there's more to the doll than meets the  eye underneath that pretty thin premise  however is a movie which is totally  willing to embrace its own silliness it  manages to spend just enough time poking  fun at itself to remain charming all the  while delivering a satisfyingly creepy  story and a solid twist ending the gift  this 2015 horror thriller written  directed by and starring Joel Edgerton  delivers on all fronts making for a  tense dramatic stalker flick that's  bound to keep you guessing to the end  Edgerton stars as Gordo a mysterious  loner who runs into an old friend from  high school  although Gordo might seem like your  typical outcast at first his sinister  intentions slowly become clear nothing  groundbreaking here then but the gift  benefits from a cast of well written  characters and a captivating approach to  morality before long you'll find  yourself questioning just who the  movie's real villain really is the tiger  hunter equal parts cheesy and sweet the  tiger hunter is the story of an Indian  immigrant in the late 70s who comes to  America in search of a job only to find  something even better a purpose it's a  total feel-good movie from start to  finish the kind of Jim best saved as an  antidote to some terrifying horror movie  a downbeat drama or anything starring  Sean Penn think of it as Prozac but with  better cinematography it's not a movie  that's going to change the world anytime  soon but you can't say it's not lovely  and sometimes that's enough  Pandora it's a story you'll probably  feel like you've heard before a nuclear  reactor goes haywire after a devastating  earthquake endangering the citizens of a  small South Korean town as various  government officials try to escape the  blame the ordinary folk do their best to  avoid the cataclysmic destruction of the  reactor itself so far so bland right  well stick around because towards the  end Pandora  suddenly transforms into something so  beautiful and touching that you can't  help but wonder if Netflix is autoplay  switch movies without you know too  seen the rest of Pandora is decent  enough but that ending is one for the  ages the perfect host david Hyde Pierce  best known for playing Niles on Frasier  here takes on a role as a high-strung  gentleman who unknowingly accepts a  criminal into his home on the eve of a  dinner party before long the script is  flipped and a whole slew of secrets  about both men are subsequently revealed  claimed Crawford co-stars as the hapless  criminal John Taylor and both he and  Pierce work hard to turn what could have  been a flat movie into a total thrill  ride the plot is riddled with twists  each building on the other until the  movie reaches a final fever pitch we  can't say much more without risking  spoilers queue it up and let it rip boys  in the trees  the events of this criminally underrated  Australian flick play out over the  course of one Halloween night as two  former friends one popular the other a  social outcasts reunite for a long walk  home filled with stories about their  childhood in their lost friendship as  each story is told boys in the trees  further embraces its McCobb fairy tale  tone reinforced by an array of colourful  visuals and anchored by the real-life  social conflicts each character faces in  their day-to-day life first time writer  director Nicolas verso balances those  two sides of the story perfectly never  allowing the fantasy to cheapen the  reality of the film or vice versa  it's both stunningly visceral and  chock-full of childhood wonder a rare  Jim indeed  [Music]
 

